{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768698-help-me-make-a-cool-gangrel","id":768698,"title":"Help me make a cool Gangrel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-18T13:23:53-08:00","id":768698,"title":"Help me make a cool Gangrel","content":"So guys, Clan Gangrel is pretty cool. Protean is a cool power, the aesthetic the Gangrel have going on is really neat, and I love the thematic of their Curse, even if mechanics can be weird. My friends and I have been planning out a setting for Las Vegas, set in present time, and I've been trying to think over a cool Gangrel character concept. I tend to prefer playing socially oriented characters, and I have made some nasty combat monsters before, so I'm wondering, what could be different and fun and very human? Does anybody have any suggestions or ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T13:38:22-08:00","id":768705,"title":"","content":"Gangrel who goes around as the Coterie's pet(s) maybe? I toyed with that idea in my mind once. Protean lets you do some fun things, and you can use every other power while you're in an animal form too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T13:53:05-08:00","id":768709,"title":"","content":"Edit: I'm embarrassed my by previous suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 03-03-2017, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T16:33:53-08:00","id":768780,"title":"","content":"Las Vegas + Gangrel makes me think of animal performance shows like Siegfried and Roy or Circus Circus.<br /> <br /> A preternaturally 'intelligent' animal (either one ghouled by the Gangrel and/or controlled by Animalism, or the Gangrel themselves) could stand to at least make a modest sum and develop some degree of local fame/notoriety. Developing Majesty would dip into the social aspect, but the audience would consistently be wowed by the performance.<br /> <br /> Many shows on the Strip and nearby go on in the evening hours, so it wouldn't be a time conflict per se, and it would be a possible way to have fun and possibly develop a Herd or Hunting Ground or other merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T17:41:02-08:00","id":768812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768698-help-me-make-a-cool-gangrel?p=768780#post768780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Las Vegas + Gangrel makes me think of animal performance shows like Siegfried and Roy or Circus Circus.<br /> <br /> A preternaturally 'intelligent' animal (either one ghouled by the Gangrel and/or controlled by Animalism, or the Gangrel themselves) could stand to at least make a modest sum and develop some degree of local fame/notoriety. Developing Majesty would dip into the social aspect, but the audience would consistently be wowed by the performance.<br /> <br /> Many shows on the Strip and nearby go on in the evening hours, so it wouldn't be a time conflict per se, and it would be a possible way to have fun and possibly develop a Herd or Hunting Ground or other merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe cause an animal show to go horribly wrong and distract security while the coterie empties out the casino vault?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T20:22:37-08:00","id":768912,"title":"","content":"I like the animal show idea.<br /> <br /> For me (and this doesn't make much sense), the combination of &quot;Gangrel&quot; and &quot;Vegas&quot; immediately made me think of Bud, Michael Madsen's character in Kill Bill.<br /> <br /> Expounding on that, I'm picturing a redneck not living up to his potential, a chew chompin', stetson wearing shit-kicker feeding off alcoholics and tweakers, a mess of a monster who's made peace with his dirty little corner of the desert. He makes his domain on a shitty, low rent trailer park that none of the more proper vampires want, maybe gets by selling drugs or operating as a pimp, manages a little retinue of blood dolls. His herd are the cast-offs, the poor blue collar slobs who get paid 7 bucks an hour to do the dirty work that keeps the magic of Vegas running, and he takes a sardonic pride in protecting them. Coyotes prowl the dusty roads around the park, and the mortal and supernatural predators that might prey on these poor schlubs know better than to venture further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 11-18-2015, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T21:42:56-08:00","id":768949,"title":"","content":"Animal control specialist. You have access to the fringes of law enforcement, you are occasionally granted access to peoples houses, you deal with animals which can be a source of Vitae as well as unique ghouls, and pounds, which can be used as a valuable commodity for supplying neonates in the city with blood. Use your Vitae cunningly and you have a nice web of connections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T22:42:54-08:00","id":768975,"title":"","content":"You said yourself you do a lot of social characters and you've made bad-ass fighters before.<br /> <br /> Make a mental character.<br /> <br /> Weird, I know, but that's the point. It's different. It's unique. And no one ever said that Gangrel HAVE to be warriors. The vampiric archetype that they embody is that of the vampire as animalistic hunter. Well, sure you have hunters like the bear who just flip out and rip you to shreds. But there are also wolves. Cunning and shrewd, who know how to leverage the resources at their disposal to take down larger foes. They're tough when they need to be, but it's the intelligence with which they hunt that makes them dangerous.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T23:39:19-08:00","id":768999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768698-help-me-make-a-cool-gangrel#post768698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what could be different and fun and very human? Does anybody have any suggestions or ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>A high-Humanity Unaligned Gangrel &quot;teenager&quot; named Summer. She considers herself to be a kind of... avatar of the spirit of senior summer, that brief hot breathless moment when the best is behind you and you're poised to leap to a <i>whole new best. </i>Huge fan of encouraging the kind of youthful drama that actually not-crap positive teen movies are made of, but most people are only lucky enough to live for a moment or two.<br /> <br /> On the downside, she can have unrealistically high expectations and is unrelentingly, sometimes insistently, positive and others can fail to meet her standards. She also indulges herself as a literal bullykiller, for those who prove overly disruptive, or for people she's found herself steering into villainous roles... and the latter is just beginning to dawn on her.<br /> <br /> When provoked, she flees, but if hounded will respond with a breathtaking savagery from ambush or a position of strength, and is comfortable playing the femme fatalle.. She's demonstrated minor mental control, animal control of the Disney-princess variety (with all the utility for savagery that entails), and on one occasion circumstantial evidence that she burst apart into a swarmform of butterflies. She is rumored to hibernate between Halloween and Valentine's Day, with the very occasional story of a holiday encounter.<br /> <br /> Very standoffish with other kindred, because they embrace their monsters so much more closely (or at least more openly), because as a (possibly) genuinely good person, she's weary of the endless violence and posturing and politicking involved in even casual contact with the Cacophany, with the exception of stark warnings for those considering harming those under her protection, or places she considers immune to the All Night Socity. She has a distant, reluctant acceptance of similarities between her beliefs and those of the LeS, but she would have to be very hard pressed to rely on them. She is sometimes sympathetic to Carthians who can spin her a tale of woeful oppression by The Man. She is rumored to have alternate supernatural connections, but beyond the assumption that they aren't deathly or destructive, no one could say what they are, apart from the usual assumptions of werewolf sympathies.<br /> <br /> As a neonate- people are taking bets on how long it's going to take her to snap and eat a whole campground before getting a dyejob and joining the Circle.<br /> <br /> As an ancillae- people are wondering how the hell it's possible for someone to have gone so long, especially in venues increasingly popular with kindred, with so few sightings, or how she maintains her facade so convincingly.<br /> <br /> As an elder- people are wondering if she really even exists, or if the storyteller/architect/lover/destroyer is some kind of kindred urban legend. Hell, is she a kindred, whatever, take your pick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I realize it doesn't exactly lend itself to playability in many ways but I just had it lying around <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 11-19-2015, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:24:53-08:00","id":769273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768698-help-me-make-a-cool-gangrel?p=768975#post768975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said yourself you do a lot of social characters and you've made bad-ass fighters before.<br /> <br /> Make a mental character.<br /> <br /> Weird, I know, but that's the point. It's different. It's unique. And no one ever said that Gangrel HAVE to be warriors. The vampiric archetype that they embody is that of the vampire as animalistic hunter. Well, sure you have hunters like the bear who just flip out and rip you to shreds. But there are also wolves. Cunning and shrewd, who know how to leverage the resources at their disposal to take down larger foes. They're tough when they need to be, but it's the intelligence with which they hunt that makes them dangerous.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Gangrel using protean to enhance his perception and to gain information, coupled with insane spying and information gathering potential of animalism can give you really fun Detective Experience, very different but still as effective as Mekhet one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T09:54:09-08:00","id":769350,"title":"","content":"You were a touchstone to a young Gangrel who really had a hard time controlling their curse. You bonded in an addiction support group or club, helping them remain human - though you never pierced the Masquerade. You had your own wild life in the past, gambling or other vices that led you to some rough, angry times. You pushed through that, working the steps, calling on higher powers. You achieved a new life for yourself. Calm, those bad times gone - or at least so suppressed there wasn't a danger of relapse. The young Gangrel turned you, wanting to give something back to you - immortality. Maybe they thought you could help others with their Feral Curse like you helped them.<br /> <br /> But now you feel the beast, you feel that curse yourself. It bubbles up in the Frenzy, in clash of predators. It's no longer suppressed, its always there, ready to explode. The steps you used - the same steps that actually helped your sire - they don't seem to help <i>you</i>, not anymore. Instead, you begin to learn about riding the wave. You learn that you can direct that ferocity, you can control it's target. And in return you get strength, power and satisfaction from your beast.<ul><li>How do you come to terms with directing and using this internal rage when you owe everything good in your once-new life to suppressing it?</li> <li>Who from that old life is <i>your</i> touchstone? How will your relationship change with them as they see what looks like you falling back to that old bad life?</li> <li>How do you feel about your sire? Do you blame them for these changes, do they become the easiest target of your beast as you learn to focus it?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T10:05:48-08:00","id":769360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768698-help-me-make-a-cool-gangrel?p=769350#post769350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You were a touchstone to a young Gangrel who really had a hard time controlling their curse. You bonded in an addiction support group or club, helping them remain human - though you never pierced the Masquerade. You had your own wild life in the past, gambling or other vices that led you to some rough, angry times. You pushed through that, working the steps, calling on higher powers. You achieved a new life for yourself. Calm, those bad times gone - or at least so suppressed there wasn't a danger of relapse. The young Gangrel turned you, wanting to give something back to you - immortality. Maybe they thought you could help others with their Feral Curse like you helped them.<br /> <br /> But now you feel the beast, you feel that curse yourself. It bubbles up in the Frenzy, in clash of predators. It's no longer suppressed, its always there, ready to explode. The steps you used - the same steps that actually helped your sire - they don't seem to help <i>you</i>, not anymore. Instead, you begin to learn about riding the wave. You learn that you can direct that ferocity, you can control it's target. And in return you get strength, power and satisfaction from your beast.<ul><li>How do you come to terms with directing and using this internal rage when you owe everything good in your once-new life to suppressing it?</li> <li>Who from that old life is <i>your</i> touchstone? How will your relationship change with them as they see what looks like you falling back to that old bad life?</li> <li>How do you feel about your sire? Do you blame them for these changes, do they become the easiest target of your beast as you learn to focus it?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow.<br /> <br /> Thanks everyone for these ideas so far, I'd love to hear more, but I just wanna say that I really love the thought you put into this, Holy. It has a level of character that really suits Las Vegas, too, while getting at the meat of a lot of stuff I find interesting about characters.<br /> <br /> Several other posts here are definitely gonna form the basis for NPCs, especially some of the weird job-based ones. I love the different ways people approach character concepts, and seeing this is really cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T14:11:19-08:00","id":769533,"title":"","content":"The Wolf of Wall St.<br /> <br /> While at a conference in Vegas, an extremely wealthy, successful businessman gets peripherally involved with the locals; rough, feral kindred who frequent the desert around Vegas more than the city itself. Think Jack Doughnegey, two floors down, without the endearing charm or occasional upper-class bumbling. Long story short, one of the locals was surprised and pleased to find out how ruthless, ingenious, and physically brutal one of the one percenters could be when their life is at stake, so they embraced him. A brief, bitter, antagonistic relationship was born between the two, based on power and the willingness to use it, which the older vampire lost pretty quickly due to its lack of familiarity with the intricacies of human civilization.<br /> <br /> Having learned something of savagery, to compliment his guile, the newly embraced corporate overachiever left his previous jet-setting lifestyle expire, being declared dead rather than try to integrate his old life into the new. He now regards Vegas with the same expression of cautious glee as a gambler at a reduced-price all-you-can-eat-buffet; an entire new setting to exploit for the sociopathic 80's business guy he used to be.<br /> <br /> The Wall St. Wolf regards himself as an ultimate darwinist, physical, mental, and social; in a society of literal predators, even the slim restraints once upon his lust for money and power have fallen away. He has risen shockingly fast through the Invictus, who accepted him originally with open arms but now are worrying that he's poised to either become a terrible threat to their internal status quo, or gradually losing himself to his Beast by constant social, supernatural, and material aggression. Worse, he understands the violence his new life often requires, with kine and other kindred, and has been enthusiastically training against the day that someone publicly challenges him, so he's no fainting boardroom blossom any longer.<br /> <br /> Neonate- while he's <i>very </i>good at what he does, he didn't have the kind of modern-world advantage he was anticipating from such secretive and ancient monsters. He'll get there, though.<br /> <br /> Ancilla- If he's not head of the local Invictus chapter, he's an advisor or agent. He's <i>just </i>where he needs to be to achieve everything he's working for.<br /> <br /> Elder- He <i>is </i>the system, and <i>don't you dare cross him</i>. If he's not running the Invictus, he's either feverishly working on his campaign for princedom, or he has his hands too full keeping the rest of the Covenant in line, or he's dead. His latest project involves finding a suitable protege, in an attempt to use the sire-childe relationship to either raise a successor, an asset, or someone to keep him sharp as per the Rule of Two. He grins wryly when thinking of his sire in that context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T10:56:30-08:00","id":770132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768698-help-me-make-a-cool-gangrel?p=768912#post768912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me (and this doesn't make much sense), the combination of &quot;Gangrel&quot; and &quot;Vegas&quot; immediately made me think of Bud, Michael Madsen's character in Kill Bill.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Doesn't make much sense&quot;? Au contraire!<br /> <br /> A lot of people envision Las Vegas as a city of lights, but having visited (repeatedly) and lived there (briefly), I can say that the Strip is only the brightest part\u2014and the brighter the lights, the darker the shadows beyond them. While a modest amount of LV is just a plain city aside from the strip, there's a whole lot of dusty wasteland out there in the dark, and no shortage of 'mobile' homes, and if you take the wrong turn on a dirt road, the desert will just close over you without a ripple.<br /> <br /> Bud the Gangrel, Trailer-Park Terror, would be perfect as a character in this environment, especially as a mental-trait-dominant one\u2014he's got more in Wits and Resolve than Intelligence, but he can smell trouble faster than a coydog can sniff out roadkill. He ain't all that sociable, and if you get down to it, he's kinda tumbleweed-y physically, but he makes up for it. Bud ain't no book-learnin' type, but he knows when to listen, when to run, and when to set up a tripwire leading to a shotgun full of rocksalt and silver dimes (&quot;Best dollar-eighty I ever spent!&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 11-20-2015, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T11:26:00-08:00","id":770156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768698-help-me-make-a-cool-gangrel?p=770132#post770132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Doesn't make much sense&quot;? Au contraire!<br /> <br /> A lot of people envision Las Vegas as a city of lights, but having visited (repeatedly) and lived there (briefly), I can say that the Strip is only the brightest part\u2014and the brighter the lights, the darker the shadows beyond them. While a modest amount of LV is just a plain city aside from the strip, there's a whole lot of dusty wasteland out there in the dark, and no shortage of 'mobile' homes, and if you take the wrong turn on a dirt road, the desert will just close over you without a ripple.<br /> <br /> Bud the Gangrel, Trailer-Park Terror, would be perfect as a character in this environment, especially as a mental-trait-dominant one\u2014he's got more in Wits and Resolve than Intelligence, but he can smell trouble faster than a coydog can sniff out roadkill. He ain't all that sociable, and if you get down to it, he's kinda tumbleweed-y physically, but he makes up for it. Bud ain't no book-learnin' type, but he knows when to listen, when to run, and when to set up a tripwire leading to a shotgun full of rocksalt and silver dimes (&quot;Best dollar-eighty I ever spent!&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks for your kind words, and you did a good job there building on the character.<br /> <br /> It's less that it doesn't fit the setting and more that it's the first place my mind went. I'm fully aware that much of Vegas is dirt and rocks and poor southwesterners eking by a living for the sake of rich tourists, but it's not the first direction one normally thinks of when someone says Las Vegas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T11:29:52-08:00","id":770157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768698-help-me-make-a-cool-gangrel?p=768999#post768999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A high-Humanity Unaligned Gangrel &quot;teenager&quot; named Summer. She considers herself to be a kind of... avatar of the spirit of senior summer, that brief hot breathless moment when the best is behind you and you're poised to leap to a <i>whole new best. </i>Huge fan of encouraging the kind of youthful drama that actually not-crap positive teen movies are made of, but most people are only lucky enough to live for a moment or two.<br /> <br /> On the downside, she can have unrealistically high expectations and is unrelentingly, sometimes insistently, positive and others can fail to meet her standards. She also indulges herself as a literal bullykiller, for those who prove overly disruptive, or for people she's found herself steering into villainous roles... and the latter is just beginning to dawn on her.<br /> <br /> When provoked, she flees, but if hounded will respond with a breathtaking savagery from ambush or a position of strength, and is comfortable playing the femme fatalle.. She's demonstrated minor mental control, animal control of the Disney-princess variety (with all the utility for savagery that entails), and on one occasion circumstantial evidence that she burst apart into a swarmform of butterflies. She is rumored to hibernate between Halloween and Valentine's Day, with the very occasional story of a holiday encounter.<br /> <br /> Very standoffish with other kindred, because they embrace their monsters so much more closely (or at least more openly), because as a (possibly) genuinely good person, she's weary of the endless violence and posturing and politicking involved in even casual contact with the Cacophany, with the exception of stark warnings for those considering harming those under her protection, or places she considers immune to the All Night Socity. She has a distant, reluctant acceptance of similarities between her beliefs and those of the LeS, but she would have to be very hard pressed to rely on them. She is sometimes sympathetic to Carthians who can spin her a tale of woeful oppression by The Man. She is rumored to have alternate supernatural connections, but beyond the assumption that they aren't deathly or destructive, no one could say what they are, apart from the usual assumptions of werewolf sympathies.<br /> <br /> As a neonate- people are taking bets on how long it's going to take her to snap and eat a whole campground before getting a dyejob and joining the Circle.<br /> <br /> As an ancillae- people are wondering how the hell it's possible for someone to have gone so long, especially in venues increasingly popular with kindred, with so few sightings, or how she maintains her facade so convincingly.<br /> <br /> As an elder- people are wondering if she really even exists, or if the storyteller/architect/lover/destroyer is some kind of kindred urban legend. Hell, is she a kindred, whatever, take your pick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I realize it doesn't exactly lend itself to playability in many ways but I just had it lying around <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This makes me want to run or play in a short term game inspired by 80s slasher films. Something out there is stalking campers. Can the survivors find out before it's too late that the real threat isn't the big furry beasts stalking the woods but is instead the bubbly teen in their midst?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T14:10:53-08:00","id":770281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768698-help-me-make-a-cool-gangrel?p=770157#post770157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me want to run or play in a short term game inspired by 80s slasher films. Something out there is stalking campers. Can the survivors find out before it's too late that the real threat isn't the big furry beasts stalking the woods but is instead the bubbly teen in their midst?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh hell yes! (Movies like <i>Tucker and Dale vs Evil </i>would be good inspiration for that, actually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}